Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.76,0:00:08.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, good afternoon everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.24,0:00:12.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,How is everyone doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.12,0:00:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have heard that this is the place to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.40,0:00:25.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Actually, this is uh AMD has been a long-standing supporter of OCP, but this is actually my first time at the OCP um Global Summit,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.79,0:00:30.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,and I have to say I'm just blown away by the scale of what uh we have here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.52,0:00:41.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I want to congratulate George and really the entire organizing committee for putting together just a fantastic event.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.72,0:00:49.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, So, today what I'd like to do is maybe talk a little bit about what we see at AMD in terms of what's happening in the market.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.62,0:00:54.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I can say for sure it's the fastest-moving market that I've ever seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.54,0:00:59.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so much uh change, so much innovation, so much collaboration.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.56,0:01:04.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And maybe from an overarching standpoint, I would say, you know, for all of us at AMD,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.68,0:01:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,we wake up every day thinking that our job is to really push the boundaries of high-performance
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.20,0:01:17.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,computing so that we can solve some of the most important challenges and problems in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.14,0:01:27.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to do this actually requires intense collaboration because I'm a big believer in there is no one company that has every answer to every solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.72,0:01:35.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And frankly, the more we can bring the best of our companies together, the better we're going to do as an industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.23,0:01:39.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, AMD has opened as a foundation of our principles.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.24,0:01:42.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's one of the things that we think about when we develop technology.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.43,0:01:45.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's one of the things that we think about when we develop our road map.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.77,0:01:51.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look at the last 15 years of what OCP has really done,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.53,0:01:57.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's really been a huge part of our development road map going first going forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.64,0:02:05.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,First on our open server platforms, from our very first platform that we did with Naples back in 2017,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.64,0:02:11.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,that was a very close collaboration with our partner Microsoft, but together we brought it to OCP.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.41,0:02:20.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you look at, you know, over the last few years, a lot of work has come together on the networking side with the Ultra Ethernet Consortium,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.16,0:02:23.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,with the work that we're doing around, you know, UALink and ESUN.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.22,0:02:27.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of those are really important things for interoperability.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.32,0:02:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm excited to talk about Helios.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.04,0:02:38.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're going to talk a little bit about Helios today and the progress on that rack scale solution, which is again based on OCP standards.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.81,0:02:44.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then looking forward, I think we have lots more opportunities to collaborate together and these also become,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.71,0:02:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,whether you're talking about MRC or Oak, these are also areas where there's just a tremendous opportunity for us to come together as an ecosystem.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.64,0:02:56.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with the notion of when we come together as an open ecosystem,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.63,0:03:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,we will actually accelerate the pace of innovation and get better solutions for our joint customers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.92,0:03:14.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, a little bit about the market, I think you guys know very well the AI market is truly transforming every part of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.21,0:03:20.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,every industry that we're in, whether you're talking about healthcare or manufacturing or science.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.25,0:03:23.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're seeing much, much more capability come across.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.97,0:03:28.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like to say that we're in a world where computing equates to intelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.93,0:03:34.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you have the chance to be more intelligent, why wouldn't you try to get more capability?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.94,0:03:39.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's really what we're trying to do in terms of bringing all of that into the ecosystem.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.01,0:03:50.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just a few of the demand numbers that you see, every time I look at these charts, they tend to keep going up into the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.28,0:03:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And people are always asking, well, you know, are we sure that we're doing productive work with all of the AI compute that we're putting on board?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.81,0:03:59.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the answer is absolutely yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.94,0:04:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we are doing a tremendous amount of work.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.04,0:04:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're getting more and more productive each time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.04,0:04:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you kind of look at some of these demand numbers and you see like a 95 x increase in tokens per month over the past 2 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.60,0:04:20.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're now at some number like almost 40 quadrillion inference tokens a month.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.50,0:04:26.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um when you think about what that means in terms of useful AI, we get a lot of different data,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.91,0:04:34.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I think the data that's most important to me is what do I see when I talk to customers and when I spend time with the largest users.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.11,0:04:35.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.11,0:04:40.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,clearly training continues to be extremely important and we're going to continue to need the largest
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.18,0:04:44.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,training clusters in the world and we're going to continue to push the envelope on capability.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.93,0:04:51.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's call it, you know, 5 x increase every year since 2020 and that doesn't look like that's going to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.99,0:04:54.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's going to continue going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.10,0:05:01.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but we've always thought that where AI really pays off is when inference overtakes training.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.86,0:05:11.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look at the numbers over the last few years, especially this year in 2026, this year is really the year of inference.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.25,0:05:18.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the year where we believe inference is now about 60% of the market going forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.60,0:05:25.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's not just inference, it's really the agentic workloads that have really taken off.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.20,0:05:27.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you look at some of these numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.54,0:05:33.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is some new data from Open Router which routes requests across many models
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.40,0:05:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,and what you see is that the amount of human traffic has gone up steadily,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.40,0:05:44.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,but what's really grown is the amount of agentic traffic and we're seeing a 14
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.79,0:05:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,x growth just this year in the amount of agentic traffic that is going through.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.48,0:05:54.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that kind of tells you the power of the of AI working.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.03,0:05:57.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is we're training better models.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.72,0:06:03.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We now have the opportunity not just to do inference, but we have the opportunity to solve problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.31,0:06:12.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with that we're seeing a lot more opportunity for growth and you know, really productive growth going forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.52,0:06:19.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, George showed some numbers about the TAM as it relates to the infrastructure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.06,0:06:28.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is some information on the the TAM as it relates to the silicon and the systems which the silicon the core which is what you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.36,0:06:29.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're focused on.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.72,0:06:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're seeing a couple things, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.20,0:06:40.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,First of all, we're seeing the data center AI accelerator TAM grow to close to 1 and 1/2 trillion by the time we get to 2030,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.64,0:06:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is a fantastically large number.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.92,0:06:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why there's so much excitement and innovation in this area.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.64,0:06:57.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we've also seen that with agentic workloads, we've seen a very significant increase in what was known as the traditional CPU TAM.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.44,0:07:03.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you were to look at this number, you know, let's call it even a year ago, you know, people would have said, "Hey,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.57,0:07:11.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,the CPU market is probably a 20 billion-dollar market growing you know, single digits over the next few years."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.46,0:07:23.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have actually raised the TAM on this three times in the last nine months because we've seen that much growth in the overall CPU demand,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.43,0:07:29.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,which we now believe will grow at approximately 50% CAGR over the next four or
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.57,0:07:34.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,five years to over a 200 billion-dollar TAM by the time you get to 2030.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.58,0:07:39.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that has implications on how you want to build systems.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.68,0:07:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The fact is, you know, there's no one size fits all when it comes to compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.88,0:07:54.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You actually need the right compute for the right workload, and that's across CPUs and GPUs and ASICs and FPGAs and all of the mix in between.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.88,0:07:59.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's the foundation of how we have, you know, really focused at AMD.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.96,0:08:07.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when you think about, you know, the three things that we think are most important, um the first and foremost is we're a compute company.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.90,0:08:09.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compute equals intelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.38,0:08:11.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need to have compute leadership.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.26,0:08:18.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that compute leadership is across, um every aspect of that, you know, CPU, GPU,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.15,0:08:23.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,ASIC, all of those capabilities because we need the right compute for each application.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.64,0:08:26.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we also believe that you're going to see AI everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.92,0:08:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're going to spend a lot of time over the next few days probably talking about the big iron, um in the cloud, hyperscale, and enterprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.64,0:08:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're big believer in the fact that you're going to see AI infused through every aspect of the edge as well as the client in the ecosystem.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.48,0:08:53.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the more that we can get the standards across those, uh those different form factors to be the same, the more that we can get the software,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.21,0:09:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh to work across all of those systems, the better off we're going to be to provide productivity to the end users of, um these systems.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.84,0:09:07.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the middle point is the point that's most relevant for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.96,0:09:11.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Open is a foundation of what we do at AMD.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.96,0:09:19.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are big, big believers, as I said, in the idea that open platforms enable collaboration.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.65,0:09:26.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Collaboration enables the best of each company to bring to the table so that we have better overall solutions.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.95,0:09:31.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the fact is, you know, AI at scale is a team sport.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.26,0:09:37.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is a an area where we want to bring, uh the the of the industry, uh together.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.79,0:09:46.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'll talk a little bit today about the work that we're doing on rack-scale innovation because it's uh been a very, very exciting uh year for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.02,0:09:52.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then a little bit about what we see going forward in terms of the agentic infrastructure.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.72,0:09:57.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you know, first and foremost, I think all all of you guys know this, but you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.69,0:10:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,this has been a principle um frontier AI has higher and higher demands on what all of us do.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.92,0:10:15.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, our job is to bring a solution to the market that allows our end users to use the technology as fast as possible,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.45,0:10:24.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,as efficiently as possible, with as little friction as possible to get the best tokens for dollar, to get the best tokens for outcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.64,0:10:26.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to do that, you need all of these pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.04,0:10:28.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to have leadership compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.02,0:10:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to have an open rack architecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.20,0:10:37.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to have um a fabric that allows you to scale uh across um the uh systems.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.68,0:10:44.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we also need to care about things like efficiency and serviceability, um as well as, you know, overall turnkey solutions.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.89,0:10:46.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you need all of these things.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.99,0:10:55.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I have to say um all of these things were critical when we decided to uh bring out the Helios uh architecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.00,0:11:00.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We launched Helios in July of this year, just a couple of months ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.40,0:11:07.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I will say, you know, our view is that this is the highest performance AI rack in the industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.64,0:11:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,72 GPUs working together as a single accelerator.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.76,0:11:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,More than 18,000 GPU compute units.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.96,0:11:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,4,600 Zen 6 cores.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.00,0:11:24.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each compute tray is just a little bit heavy um at uh 160 lb.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.84,0:11:28.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the total rack is nearly 7,000 lb.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.32,0:11:33.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um it's a little bit of a machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.40,0:11:41.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think George said something like everyone gets a little wider as the years pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.92,0:11:44.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I don't want to say that about our racks,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.49,0:11:56.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I would say we made a very deliberate choice with Helios uh to use the um OCP um open rack wide standard.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.09,0:12:03.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it is uh one of the most ambitious engineering feats that I've ever had a chance to be part of in my career.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.45,0:12:06.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this was co-engineered with Meta, um our partner.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.32,0:12:09.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know you're going to hear from Santosh a little bit later on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.30,0:12:12.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I have to say it has been a tremendous partnership.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.81,0:12:18.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know, we started with the notion of look, there going to be a lot of accelerators out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.41,0:12:20.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it is not one-size-fits-all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.64,0:12:23.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not you know, one company has all the best parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.00,0:12:29.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we want to do is make it really easy for a heterogeneous data center environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.75,0:12:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cuz there's a firm belief in that you're going to need a mix of CPUs, GPUs, uh purpose-built ASICs.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.36,0:12:41.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're going to want to be in a similar data center environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.26,0:12:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're not going to want to switch out every component every time you change an accelerator.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.57,0:12:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're really going to try to to standardize as much as you can so that you are differentiating on the things that make the most difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.40,0:13:00.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's exactly what we've done with um the Helios platform together with Meta.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.34,0:13:06.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think what we see here is um a tremendous opportunity to bring the ecosystem together.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.02,0:13:16.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, lots and lots of partners are needed to make Helios happen, but it includes um the uh open architecture on the rack standpoint,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.59,0:13:21.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,um open uh power shelves, open networking, and the overall management system.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.99,0:13:26.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're very uh happy with how Helios uh uh has come along.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.50,0:13:31.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um as part of this, uh networking is a huge piece of this ecosystem.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.09,0:13:35.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would say that we've spent um quite a bit of time internally, you know, for us,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.59,0:13:42.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh Norrod who runs the data center solutions for us, in terms of architecting this thing, um whole thing coming together.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.31,0:13:46.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, our principle is we wanted to use the best solution that was available.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.18,0:13:52.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the best solution that would be was available would mean bringing in uh the leading networking partners in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.54,0:13:57.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're doing tremendous work with Broadcom, Cisco, Arista, HPE, DriveNets.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.35,0:14:05.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the idea is to have leading front-end solution, um leading scale-up solution with uh UALink over Ethernet,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.31,0:14:11.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,as well as ESUN, and then leading scale-out solutions, um as well, that are uh ahead of the industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.43,0:14:16.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of this is delivered through the OCP open ecosystem.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.08,0:14:21.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of this um openness extends to software, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.12,0:14:32.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the idea of software is, you know, we need to make for that it's super easy for our customers to bring new workloads onto our accelerators.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.16,0:14:37.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to do that, you want to have, let's call it, the leading open communities running natively.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.63,0:14:42.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have the top 15 open AI communities that are supporting AI AMD natively.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.94,0:14:45.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have seen uh significant benefit.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.63,0:14:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perhaps this is one of the largest benefits that we've seen of AI.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.72,0:14:58.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is a case where, you know, agentic AI can actually continue to make the performance of the hardware um better over time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.64,0:15:05.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh just to give you one uh statistic, um Hyperloom is our agentic AI solution,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.48,0:15:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we've had it running continuously running for uh the Hugging Face models.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.44,0:15:20.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, over 14,000 models on Hugging Face with no humans in the loop, we've seen almost a 40% improvement in performance just having the agentic AI run.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.70,0:15:30.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the key is open ecosystems on hardware, software bringing the opportunity to get significant performance uh capability to our end users.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.76,0:15:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, if you take a look at all of those pieces, what does that mean to the end user?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.44,0:15:42.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,The Helios rack delivers um the highest compute in the industry, the highest memory uh capacity,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.33,0:15:49.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,the highest memory bandwidth, and the highest networking uh capacity or capability across um the industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.95,0:16:01.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to give you some idea of the numbers, uh we believe that uh we're translating into 30% more tokens per dollar using uh the Helios uh solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.44,0:16:04.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, all the PowerPoint sounds great.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.36,0:16:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's probably better to see a few pictures.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.08,0:16:07.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.41,0:16:08.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,um let me show
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.66,0:16:09.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,you a
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.16,0:16:09.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,little
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.75,0:16:10.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,bit
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.08,0:16:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.52,0:16:50.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,People told me that rack-scale solutions would be the hardest thing that we've ever done.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.10,0:16:52.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think they were absolutely right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.85,0:17:01.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Helios is absolutely uh the most uh sophisticated and complex system that we have built um at AMD together with our partners.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.29,0:17:05.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh but I'm very happy to say that Helios is in production today.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.28,0:17:08.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we started shipping production in September.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.36,0:17:16.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first systems are installed at our leading customers, OpenAI, Meta, Micro System uh Microsoft, um Oracle,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.00,0:17:25.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anthropic, and we continue to see just tremendous learnings when we bring all of these these pieces together.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.79,0:17:31.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, our production will continue to ramp through the fourth quarter into the first half of next year, but what we did is,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.35,0:17:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, with the OCP standard working together with our partners was just fantastic engineering overall.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.20,0:17:44.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm happy to say there's significant growing adoption of Helios, not only the largest model companies,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.69,0:17:50.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,but in addition a number of AI native companies, a number of the overall ecosystem ODMs, OEMs.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.65,0:17:53.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know a bunch of you are in the audience today.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.67,0:17:55.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Neoclouds, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.36,0:17:57.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for all of the collaboration on Helios.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.61,0:18:05.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to continue to broaden this going forward as we, you know, think about, you know, the next next few quarters.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.32,0:18:11.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, with that, maybe I'll transition a little bit to agentic infrastructure.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.64,0:18:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I would say that this is probably the place where that has been the most activity over the last let's call it 6 months or so.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.16,0:18:23.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's been a lot of talk about agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.31,0:18:25.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would say the excitement is real.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.15,0:18:31.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we've all seen just tremendous productivity whether in personal use cases or
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.49,0:18:37.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the in enterprise use cases and it's moving much faster than we thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.43,0:18:41.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, kind of some of the examples out there that are pretty interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.28,0:18:49.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, Muse has kind of recaptured the imagination as to what AI can do for the consumer.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.09,0:18:54.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,This number of 5 million downloads of Meta Muse was as of the end of September.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.58,0:18:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that was like the first, you know, couple weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.20,0:18:59.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sure Santosh will talk about it more.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.28,0:19:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think I read this morning in the Wall Street Journal that they're down to now up to 9 million downloads of Meta Muse in just the first month or so.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.00,0:19:16.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, OpenAI has talked about using um, 10,000 agents to solve some of the most difficult math problems um,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.88,0:19:20.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,in uh, history that haven't, you know, really seen the full uh, solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.77,0:19:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anthropic talks about using R&D agents to uh, really get a quad working.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.28,0:19:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these say that agentic usage is real.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.28,0:19:37.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can tell you within AMD, we're actively using agents both on our silicon development as well as on our software development.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.29,0:19:39.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,I gave you the example of Hyperloom.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.03,0:19:47.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you say, "Okay, everyone talks about agents, but what do you actually need uh, for agents?"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.19,0:19:53.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think the most important thing to realize is that agents actually are not one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.70,0:19:57.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, agents, like people, there are lots of different types of agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.41,0:20:01.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need the right agents for the right um, application.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.32,0:20:04.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for that, you actually need the right compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.21,0:20:09.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when you're talking about personal agents, you probably want the densest agents possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.64,0:20:14.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are simpler tasks, and you want them to be uh, you know, very efficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.67,0:20:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want them to be maximum number of agents per watt, so you are uh, saving your power correctly.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.64,0:20:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, you know, that's one class of agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.96,0:20:28.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, you talk about enterprise agents, where you're doing a lot of different types of activities, and so you want them to be pretty balanced.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.08,0:20:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or you're talking about some of the hardest compute problems out there, these technical compute agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.76,0:20:38.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going You're going to want them to be bleeding-edge performance, kind of the the best of the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.69,0:20:42.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, each of these agents needs a different type of compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.54,0:20:48.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we believe is each of these agents also need the right type of rack.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.11,0:20:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that means you're going to see a certain type of rack in hyperscale environments, where you might have disaggregated CPU and GPU racks.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.68,0:21:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whereas in enterprise, you might want to see more all-in-one racks uh, going forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.36,0:21:09.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'm happy to say this morning, we announced um, the AMD Helion Agentic AI Rack.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.10,0:21:12.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Helion is the cousin to Helios.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.20,0:21:19.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh it's really focused on the Agentic AI compute um aspect of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.21,0:21:26.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh what we're trying to do here is frankly do what is easiest in terms of bringing all of the
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.50,0:21:34.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,pieces of the Open Compute um infrastructure together so that we can get the most efficient uh CPU uh racks.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.19,0:21:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that is you can use the you can use a combination of CPUs and GPUs.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.16,0:21:43.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're also um we're also integrating it with a token router.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.67,0:21:51.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think everyone is talking about how can you most efficiently uh route your um overall AI usage.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.27,0:21:59.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know that within our own IT infrastructure, uh the idea is you don't need the same model for every question.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.13,0:22:01.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't need the same compute for every question.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.66,0:22:08.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want to be able to route uh the right model and the right compute for the right um application.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.09,0:22:13.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's a key piece of this as well as the overall um open environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.64,0:22:22.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, a few of the things about our Helion um Agentic AI Rack, um the nice thing about Helion is we've used uh you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.24,0:22:31.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,practically everything that we could through um OCP's OCP specs uh with the idea of it's a standard 21-inch rack.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.27,0:22:33.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can be liquid or air cooled.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.73,0:22:42.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is up to 32,000 plus Zen 6 cores, which is 40% more than the other competitive racks.
